---
title: "A partnership without a motion is a favor"
description: "If pipeline dies when you stop texting, you don't have a partner. You have a friend with a logo."
date: "2026-07-14"
tags:
  - partnerships
  - growth
published: true
layout: docs
---

Want the fastest way to waste a quarter? Collect logos and call it distribution.

Our clearest early win at Algility was not a dashboard. It was partners that moved money.

On a 2024 B2B push with SINT Protocol, the work was enterprise growth and a partner ecosystem. What mattered Monday: closed partners, qualified pipeline, real conversations. Not a slide with brands on it.

Same pattern every loud month since. New partners show up. Ads get louder too. Only one of those shortens trust.

A good partner already has the buyer's attention. Your job is to turn that attention into a repeatable intro. Not a coffee. A motion.

Keep a partnership only if it clears three checks.

1. Shared customer. Not shared press.
2. Repeatable intro. Not one warm chat.
3. Clear ownership when a lead goes cold.

If it dies the week you stop babysitting the calendar, it was never a partnership. It was a favor wearing a logo.

Favors feel good. Motions print.
